In a normal cuda inference server context, an instance of the connected GRAPH would be kept running if 10 requests come in within the same time. Each GRAPH requires 2 GB of RAM that is available with most inference GPU - either intel’s grazie or mnvc.

But if the inference invitation instance was created with cuDAGRAF library - ie with dynamic batching feature. Then the 10 instances would be coalesced together by an inference scheduler and only one x-to-nx sized instance accepted.

In this case there would be only 1 GRAPH running for all the threads and next cycle hence on would find that only 2 GB of RAM is being used

