```

While the event is clear and the generator is processing a packet, other packets will wait adding memory to the generator queue. After the generator sets the event and processes packets in multiprocessing, the original blocking gpu protection cancels and callback empties the queue and clears the event for the next packet. The result is that callback ignores packets while “in-processing” and the grpc server has fewer gpu switch calls.

