[58/200] Running: Describe an RLHF (Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback...

🧠 LLM Response:


Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback (RLHF) is a technique to train an AI model such that it is optimized for human preferences. This requires a human in the loop. The whole (much simplified) process can be described in the following steps.

- Train a model that is optimized for predicting the next word, given a text prompt (i.e, given “Is the cat a good boy? Yes, because”, what is the next word most likely to appear?).
- Show samples of the model’s outputs to humans and ask them to rank the samples. For example, you can ask: “Which of the following answers was more insightful: A or B?”. The samples are ranked by randomizing repeatedly and thus a preference $P(query B \gt query A)$ is established.
- Train a RL model that optimizes for higher probability of selection by the human. Backpropagate the RL loss through the RL model and the base language model.

RLHF is used to fine-tune OpenAI’s language models (e.g. for ChatGPT) and is used in conjunction with InstructGPT. ^{1}
