[64/200] Running: What is model checkpointing and resumption?...

🧠 LLM Response:


- You can save a checkpoint file to capture trainable parameter states for model variables and perform a warm start with these checkpoints on a new session.
- Model state (both trainable and non-trainable parameters) can be also saved to a checkpoint (with or without training) to be restored later.

The following instructions demonstrate the basic steps for model checkpointing and resumption in frames. By following the instructions below, you can start with a new session, perform a number of training iterations, save a checkpoint for the model for warm start, and restore the saved checkpoint for warm start from the previous step.

1) Start a new session

```
frames -open 1
```

2) Create a new model in the running session

```
model.new()
```

3) Perform a number of training iterations with the model

```
model.train_iterations 10
```

4) Create a new model in the running session

```
model.new()
```

5) Set Save Mode to Save All

```
model.save_mode all
```

6) Save model checkpoint at iteration 0

```
model.save()
```

7) Set Save Mode to No Save

```
model.save_mode no_save
```

8) Set Init Restore to Yes

```
model.init_restore yes
```

9) Set Restore Iteration

```
model.restore_iteration 0
```

10) Run resumption

```
model.restore()
```
