2. Local validation: the entire model is on one device for proper evaluation.

Coordinator checkpoints (and client delta updates) and replicates the model before training. The `tf.distribute.StrategyExtended` embedded in the server training process will coordinate saving the model via `tf.train.Checkpoint`, likely by saving part of the model from one replica and ignoring the others:

- TF 2.11: training strategy saves the model via hooks.
- TF 2.12: signature local validation/training use the `saving_listeners` of a partitioned model.

