🧠 LLM Response:

Proteus, AHA’s networking software framework that handles network connectivity and communications, is an integral part of the Gaudi server solution from Habana Labs. The software stack consists of Proteus, a Qualcomm network interface card (NIC), and Tomahawk® 2 Terabit Ethernet Switch System, working together to deliver efficient distributed training.

What is RDMA?
RDMA refers to Remote Direct Memory Access, which allows applications direct memory access to other systems on the network bypassing the buffer copying in kernel memory eliminating the buffer copy and context switch associated with regular socket-based communication. The Proteus software accelerates the DPU using bRdma (RDMA for bonded NICs) to achieve high bandwidth and with very low latency.

Where and why is RDMA used?
RDMA is a specific byte stream transfer semantic supported by some transports like RoCE, InfiniBand, and IWARP. The motivation behind RDMA is to increase performance for distributed applications by removing bottlenecks and reducing CPU utilization in the communication layers.

Habana Labs presentation: Scale Deep Learning Services & AI Applications across racks in the Cloud

What is bRdma, a resilient RDMA implementation over bonded NICs and InfiniBand?
bRdma (RDMA for bonded NICs) is a high-performance RDMA-compliant communication software service that supports resilient bonded ports for any network adapter to enable server-to-server communications over software-configurable modes. The bRdma v2.0 service is for RoCE, which is based on Ethernet but uses bonding or LACP (Link Aggregation Control Protocol), an IEEE 802.1AX standard. When the LACP is used to combine multiple ports into one bigger pipe, it has reduced performance when the bonded ports are on the same switch (SW) because the traffic will egress and only come back on the same SW port, hence, reducing utilization to less than 50%.

bRdma v2.0 technology increases bandwidth and performance by eliminating such performance bottlenecks. At the same time, it reduces complexity by enabling VLAN tagged bonding. It enables higher resiliency for fault-tolerant networking by supporting NIC failures. bRdma is a Linux kernel module that bypasses the host CPU and communicates  with the chip directly. This allows bRdma service to gain direct access to hardware acceleration features which provides low latency and higher throughput with the same message size compared to using the regular TCP/IP sockets.

Why is bRdma important to address challenges of today’s cloud infrastructure?

- The online services and AI applications must cope with intense data volume and high velocity tools.
- Growing network traffic overloads traditional data center architectures.
- Central processing units (CPUs) are overloaded, thereby negatively impacting performance and service delivery.
- In-rack rack traffic has doubled every three years, and rack units are associated with a bottleneck.
- As a workload grows, every additional server comes with a cross-sectional bandwidth utilization increase of approximately 7x.

bRdma has modular architecture and value proposition for cloud network operators.
This was precisely the problem statement presented by Mark Nossokoff, an Assistant Professor in the Department of Computer Science at the University of Wisconsin, Eau Claire, along with his PhD candidate Alexander Amies, at the 34^{th} IEEE/ACM Symposium on Parallelism in Algorithms and Architectures (SPAA), which took place in Lyon, France, last July. The research was sponsored by the U.S. National Science Foundation (NSF), Habana Labs and Xilinx.

“Our research shows how Proteus RDMA improves in-rack data traffic originating from multiple high performance data center servers that satisfy a query from a separate rackult trace file to achieve a performance of up to two orders of magnitude improvement while using Proteus.  The performance was achieved while transferring equal-size messages distributed across multiple server racks,” Nossokoff said. “This virtual outcome demonstrates that inter-rack and intra-rack data traffic can benefit from RDMA when installed in an offload model, particularly when a variety of active queries need to be accommodated. The entry points of the research represent the top 2020 Hot Cloud research topics of interest for cloud networking, and it continues to be a tracker of original research in the field.

