At some point it may become clear that some variable doesn’t meaningfully influence performance, at which point it can be fixed at some value close to the optimum given the others. Generally speaking, however there tends to be diminishing returns, for spending time searching the property space — so I’d be liberal about what “close to optimum” means.

Finally, the oversight team reviewing results needs to watch for signs that results are nonmonotonic. This could indicate a performance bug; it could also be a bug in the test framework where the current output mode of operation is different from the output coming ultimately from an Integration test with HUDI at the head using the same stream parameters.
