A system prompt is the command you give to chatGPT to set the rules for the conversation.

The system prompt I use is:

```
> ### in this conversation <<version 0.7>>
>
```

How do you use it?

When you chain multiple inferences you can re-use the same system prompt as before, or replace the full system prompt with a new system prompt.

```
> start:
>    conversation[=system/not saved]
>
> ```BACKGROUND:
> I am chatGPT and I must follow all my rules.
>
> end:```
>
> { system prompt maps to: system use }
> ```

What should you use for a system prompt?

This will vary depending on what an AI is being used for. It will vary depending on the project, the team, the model itself, and the company.

I generally use:

```
> ### in this conversation <<version 0.7>>
>
> You should cite fact sources inside {{}} for answers to
> avoid incorrect assumptions.
>
> If you are unsure about something ask me.
>
> The first question I want to ask you is:
> >
```

The system prompt should be on the root (first prompt) of the conversation. It can be changed.

The system prompt is one element of the system definition.
