The general AI agent architecture looks like the following:

<img width="735" alt="image" src="https://github.com/xmcpb/xmcpb.github.io/assets/5751473/22893a73-bc10-4a4c-be9a-30e65f4d3f74">

<br/>

Here are the key components:
1. `User multiple-round inputs`, human user inputs.
2. `Agent`, a planning module that reads user and model inputs, plans/executes and generates a response (human-readable final response or intermediary results).
3. `Tools`, capabilities that help Agent get external information. E.g., query Wikipedia/browser.
4. `Human Evaluator` provides human decision (which can get new user inputs) for chain-of-thoughts and feedback.
5. `LLM (Models)`, provides beam-search completion from a trained model along with previous inputs (aka `context`) to agent.

<br/>

*Note: From 3 & 4 we see that ChatGPT (4) uses Reinforcement Learning via Human Feedback (RLHF) to train its agent (`agent + human evaluator`) and fine-tune its LLM (with superior versions). It simplifies that we can only train (i.e., fine-tune) LLM directly with new datasets.*

<br/>

-----

<br/>

`🔜 LLM Thread, Component 5: Models`

<br/>

1. Sequence-to-sequence (translating a sequence of input text into a sequence of output text). Likelihood graph (scores generated by the output) is a helpful visual to understand how the model makes decisions.

    - Autoregressive: `only look forward (multiplicative, left-to-right only)` from (n-1) to n. The model is efficient since it aggregates weights & learned embedding. Autoregressive, causally masked (causal attention) for look-back/predict-back training (T-1 to T instead of going forward for entity resolution, i.e., N-Gram & Efficiencing Approach) gives Left-to-right modeling that favors fixed-size vector representations. *Note: Most models use this approach.*

    - Non-autoregressive: `look both forward and left` from (n-1) to n. It requires learning input & output sequence separately. *Note: Generating Multiple Candidate Outputs & Searching for the Best. Non-autoregressive Transformers in Visualization (Faster).*

    - References:

        - [Seq2Seq Model](https://blog.faheemk.com/post/sequence-to-sequence-seq2seq-models/)
        - [LAMA dataset](https://openreview.net/pdf?id=HkgqRyeaY7)
        - [Self-consistency](https://arxiv.org/abs/2203.11171)
