## What are attention scores and how are they computed?

Once your simulation finishes running, you automatically receive an Attention Score for every Digital Element (Text, Imagery, Design, Videos, Audio, Page Layout). The Attention Score shows how quickly and to what extent any element grabs attention. It’s expressed in a range from 0-100%. Gaze tracking is usually needed to understand attention but with Saccade you can easily and cost-effectively understand user attention, and it’s more accurate than traditional gaze tracking.

- The Attention Score is an accuracy and time score combined, and it’s calculated from the dot-cursor data of your simulation participants.
- The higher the attention score, the faster and with more accuracy your simulation participants were able to find the element on your creative or website.

We calculate specific attention scores including:

- Attention Speed: This is an indication of whether or not the element was found quickly (Speed Imagine speed dating…  Better speed scores mean faster attention.
- Attention Quality: This score reflects accuracy. The higher the quality of user attention, the higher the score.

## Top-ranking elements

Anytime you click the Visibility Comprehension map sensor, the attention scores appear next to every element. They are also displayed below the Comprehension Results table. This table displays all the elements in order, top-down, from the element that was found and understood best, to those that your respondents were not able to locate or understand. For example, if you test three product webpages, the product slogan will receive a score, and each individual product will receive a score, as well as the navigation bar, product pictures, etc.
There may be subtle differences in the attention score based on how the user evaluates your content. In this way you can quickly see if the headline is more noticeable, or maybe a color variation was more likely to grab attention.

- Remember: test with real people -where and how you ask your question can also influence the results!

