CLIP (which doesn’t work out of the box as said by others) is OpenAI’s version but for images and text and the title is awesome: learning transferable visual models from natural language supervision. FYI CLIP uses a vision transformer called “ViT-B/32″ so it is basically using BERT’s transformer architecture but with images instead.

So learning natural supervision from images is a fancy way to say you create 2 words (car, no-car) and you feed these samples (images with “car” or images with “no-car”) into the model and it guesses if the image is more like “car” or “no-car”. They trained that model and gave the code.

