[135/200] Running: How to compute throughput with variable prompts?...

🧠 LLM Response:


Hi,

We are experiencing a problem with the computation of the throughput in the analyzer.

Files have a variable amount of prompts. They are all mandatory. When they are asked, there is no difference with the values found in the answers in the recording, this step is correctly passed by JMeter.
But the next step is always paused for all the answers to be given because the server is still trying to get the arrow prompts.
In other words, if 3 keystrokes are needed, the last keystroke will be ignored and JMeter will wait 3.5 seconds (= vsam exit time) before advancing to the next prompt.

However in the recording of this step, no keystrokes are sent, as you know you don't have to push through terminal input buffers when the next step gets fetched without any [Enter] in between.

To bypass the problem with stepped-in input buffers, you can add the setting "Terminal Input" = PUSH in the scenario, but this pushes every keystroke from every answer and that slows the general processing dramatically, since each step has to wait for the input buffers to be pushed.
This is not sustainable, because in reality, steps just fetch answers from the terminal and don't do unnecessary user-initiated CICS I/O.

We uploaded a simple example of this behavior on BLU Age support platform and even more interesting we gave you an alternative "press ENTER in the prompt" script.
As you can see there still is a pause of 1 second on 42. There is no instruction that would justify this delay.

See APM44014 for more details
