 Jason Yosinski approached me about 5 years ago, because he was interested in the mechanistic interpretability of positional encoding and attention. He disappeared into industry after that, but I just noticed that his project presented something of interest: his work was the first to use the “positional encoding encodes continuous information about positions” methodology that we’ve seen recently.

