What is ensemble learning?
    Ensemble learning, a basic machine learning paradigm, uses multiple learning algorithms to solve a single problem to achieve better accuracy than a single model can achieve. Some examples of ensemble learning are bagging, boosting, and stacking. Voting regression, voting classifier, random forest, AdaBoost are the most widely used ensemble learning algorithms used in machine learning.
What types of ensemble models are supported?
    The Deep Learning service supports only versions of Voting Model Ensembling (VME).
Do I need to manually create an ensemble to use the general availability (GA) service?
    No. The Watson Machine Learning (WML) users no longer need to create and manage an ensemble model. They now see the automatically created ensemble model directly on the WML user interface.
Can I replace a deployed ensemble model?
    Yes, you can replace a deployed ensemble model, just like any other deployed model. However, you must be a premium plan user to use this feature.
How do I check to see what models are available in the Deep Learning service?
