    - Deployed automatically created ensemble model by default
    - Support to automatically train upon base scoring models
    - Endpoint returned when an ensemble model is deployed successfully
Is it true that I will be able to access the prediction results of the base models for an ensemble model ID?
    No, the prediction results of the base models will be accessible only if the user enabled the `logoutput` option while deploying the base model.
What about deploying an ensemble model in runtime upon base models?
    The service takes care of creating, training, and deploying an ensemble model automatically. Automatically deployed ensemble models will have a maximum of five base models associated if the model type is classifier. If its type is regressor, it has only two base models associated. Similarly, image models with type classifier will have a maximum of ten base models, and image models with type regressor will have only five base models.
