How to get per-prompt metrics in our application logs?

Environment:

Chat Prompt Latency
Oracle B2C Service, versions September 2016 and newer

Resolution:

For each end-user prompt sent, the IBM Watson logic computes its intent, entities, and dialog nodes, and takes certain actions and generates a response message.

When Oracle Service Chatbot Engine does not use IBM Watson logic to compute intent, entities, recursive database queries, and/or dialog nodes, the per-operation latency can be seen in the application log. For examples, when Session start/update/end IBM Watson logic is needed, or when session stored data is used to compute arguments, the per-prompt latency cannot be seen in logs.

In the Web Chat Intent Flow Log, the following log records can be seen to determine the end-to-end latency. The last Watson End Point details and overall prompting latency.

0: {coordinator args: {dbs: db action}}
     sis_start - overall Watson latency start (ms)
     query_end - overall Watson latency end (ms)

1: {Coordinator db args: {dbs: db action}}
     sis_start - overall Watson DB latency start (ms)
     query_end - overall Watson DB latency end (ms)

2: {Arguments}

3: {Watson Endpoint Arguments}

4: {Watson Endpoint Details}

session id: <Provides session end-to-end latency details>
session id_endpointId: <Provides latency details for Siri and CB APIs>
>>>>emulatedArguments: <Provides latency details for Dialog node API>

5: {Watson Endpoint response}

Processing Time: 000000 <Provides latency details for Dialog node API>
