Hi @Sambit,

Thanks for your question. We provided token logits directly to simplify research prototyping. For instance, you do not need to grab raw logits out of a model, compute exponentials, and 0th out a few log values by hand. Indeed even with raw log-probs, it is scary how many bugs I wrote in C++ doing that!

You can convert token logits into log-probs by using this formula (where ! symbol indicates functional-programming-safe discrete set index and square brackets is the value of the function at that index):

\[ y\left[i\right]=-\mathrm{log}\left(\sum _{j\ne i}{e}^{x\left[j\right]}\right) \]

Because these bounds are so well-known, our client assumed this was sufficient. I’m happy to make it a FAQ or update the client code. We are continuing to upgrade our docs.

Best,
Vincent

