🧠 LLM Response:


###### FAQ #101774

With the configuration of the Buffer Waiting time it is not possible to determine the exact TTFT (Time to first tweet) on the PCD3.G1x00.

Description

For PCD2’s it is well known how to measure the TTFT (Time to first tweet). The PCD3.G1x00 provides a tweeter interface too but it does not allow a reasonable count of the time to first tweet.

Solution

Apart from benchmark tests an exact TTFT measurement cannot be performed since all digital (parallel) input starts with a scan to the physical I/O. The time for the LAN communication link cannot be measured separately.  Nevertheless, it can be said, that a first tweet is performed within 8 - 10 ms.

With CBX-terminals being connected to a M1x20, the TTFT is below 3 ms.

Remark

Some I/O Interfaces of the PCD3 series like the CBX or the Serial Interface module allow a transport TX method which guarantees a deterministic TTFT.
Please see FAQ 101673 to get more information on the deterministic TTFT (Time To First Tweet).

