Reinforcement learning is a learning method inspired by the reward and punishment mechanism. There are specific optimal actions associated with every situation. It aims at finding relation between a situation and actions that would maximize the reward or minimize risk. It learns through experience. It is inspired by the biological mechanism to learn behavior basing on past experience.
Some situations require a precise action. For example, when you play football you know running behind the ball and kicking it is not any good. You have to play football carefully with proper tactics. Only when a player achieves a goal, they are rewarded. Even a small gain is a reward and loss is a punishment. All soccer players know the ground rules and they just play as per the optimum strategy which is a big part of reinforcement learning.
Similarly, a Thermostat reduces the use of cooling or heating systems when they find the air condition is approaching the set temperature. So, in that case, we can understand that you either have to cool the air or heat the air. If you over cool, you waste energy so you need to create a balance because there’s a reward associated with the appropriate action and punishment associated with an inappropriate action.
Q23. What is a customization layer in H2O?
Ans. H2O uses a layer called ‘domino’ which is a customization layer between the browser and actual web-servers. Domino consists of basic services and processes such as routing, queuing, authentication, security, caching, logging, and auditing data. This acts as a computer architecture as it holds all the services for effective functioning and each service is implemented as a web application that acts as a web container. You can achieve near infinite horizontal scalability for users and implementations using domino
