 What are the strengths and weaknesses of each?

## A.

GPT is an openAI architecture that is used for natural language processing (NLP). It was developed by Google and is the basis for Google Assistant. The use of GPT is often considered to be the de facto standard for NLP. However, other architectures exist, including BERT, which was designed by Microsoft Research.

BERT is a deep learning architecture that was designed for NLP. It is a recurrent neural network (RNN) that uses convolutional neural networks (CNNs). The use of CNNs allows BERT to learn from small context windows that are easy to parallelise on GPUs. The architecture was introduced in October 2018 and has been used since then.

Because GPT uses small context windows, it tends to be better at understanding short statements or sentences. It also has a limited vocabulary, meaning that it cannot handle some words or phrases that BERT can handle very well.

BERT is usually better than GPT at understanding longer statements or texts. It has a larger vocabulary with more fluid and natural sounding responses. However, because it uses larger context windows than GPT, it can also be more expensive to build as it requires more memory and more data for training.

## B.

GPT-3 is a neural network that uses the transformer architecture. BERT is also a neural network that uses the transformer architecture. The difference is in their training. GPT-3 was trained using a lot of unsupervised text while BERT was trained using a lot of supervised text.. Both networks have their own strengths and weaknesses. GPT-3 has more vocabulary than BERT because it was trained on larger corpora of machine-generated text. This means that it is able to understand complex language patterns better than BERT which was trained on small amounts of manually annotated data..
You can use GPT-3 for tasks such as question answering, text classification, sentiment analysis, language translation and summarization..
Another advantage of GPT-3 is that it can be used for tasks such as generating natural language sentences or text from machine-generated images. This is because it can understand context from languages other than English and use them to generate text..
GPT-3 has a high computational cost because it needs more data to train on.. On the other hand, BERT has a lower cost since it does not need as much data to train on..
An example of a task that can be performed using GPT-3 is question answering.. In this case, you would use it to understand the meaning of a sentence or question rather than just answering it.

